# Secrets — never commit. Present from the first commit, ahead of the M3 dotenv loader.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated artifacts
outputs/
logs/

# IR generated from a real specification. The brief treats the IR as a reviewable artifact that
# belongs in git, and in general it should be - but IR parsed from a real spec carries live URLs
# and infrastructure names, so it stays untracked until there is a rule for what is safe to
# commit. Same open question as probe-record redaction; not one to answer by default.
# Synthetic fixture IR under tests/fixtures/ir/ is unaffected and stays tracked.
data/ir/

# Probe records: real request and response payloads.
data/probe/

# Hand-built reference scripts. docs/reference/pkce_entra_reference.jmx carries a live Entra
# tenant id, a client id, an internal hostname and a scope naming a client's service - the same
# class of thing data/ir/ is excluded for, and this repository is public. The findings taken from
# it are written up in CLAUDE.md in general terms; the file itself stays local. Untracked from the
# start, and absent from every commit - keep it that way rather than committing and reverting.
docs/reference/

# Local working clone of the pipeline repo, created by `perfgen publish`. Someone else's
# repository checked out inside this one - it is not ours to track, and committing it would nest a
# second git history here. Listed ahead of the code that creates it, same as .env and data/probe/.
.perfgen/

# JMeter run artifacts
jmeter.log
*.jtl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
